\f0\fs24 \cf0 PROJECT DESCRIPTION\
\
This project analyzes the Artificial Intelligence Jobs Market dataset from 2025\'962026. The dataset contains around 1,500 job postings across 14 countries and 25 different AI-related roles.\
\
The goal of this project is to build a machine learning model that can predict the salary of an AI job based on various features such as job role, country, company size, and industry.\
\
The dataset is first loaded and explored using Python libraries such as Pandas and NumPy. Categorical data such as job roles and country names are converted into numerical form using Label Encoding so that machine learning algorithms can process them.\
\
The data is then divided into training and testing sets using the train-test split method. A Random Forest Regression model is trained on the training dataset to learn patterns between the input features and salary values.\
\
After training the model, predictions are made on the test dataset. The model performance is evaluated using regression metrics such as Mean Absolute Error (MAE), Mean Squared Error (MSE), and R\'b2 Score.\
\
This project helps understand salary trends in the AI job market and demonstrates how machine learning can be used to predict salaries based on job-related features.}